# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Withheld from the public release
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The two bamsort read-extraction scripts are available on request, not
# distributed. See PRIVATE_SCRIPTS.md. Every script that invokes them checks
# first and exits with a message pointing there.
# Matched by basename, not by path, so moving them inside the tree cannot
# quietly un-ignore them (a path-anchored rule did exactly that once).
bamsort_alignment_reads.py
bamsort_alignment_reads_host.py

# Python bytecode. This matters more than it looks: a .pyc decompiles back to
# readable source, so a committed __pycache__ would publish the scripts above.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Run artifacts, not source
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SLURM stdout/stderr from this lab's own runs. They carry absolute paths and
# account names and say nothing a reader needs. The glob is `logs*/` because one
# of them is `logs_intron1000/` -- a plain `logs/` missed 51 files.
logs*/
*.log
*.out
*.err
# and any stray <name>_<jobid>.txt left outside a logs dir
*_[0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9].txt

# Exploratory one-off harnesses: they pull chunk bodies out of the notebooks to
# re-run a single analysis, and are not part of the published pipeline.
plotScripts/.runs/

# R and editor byproducts
Rplots.pdf
.Rhistory
.RData
.Rproj.user/
*.Rproj
.DS_Store
